Seq66 macro: ping

# The Identity Request packet is the de facto "ping" command in the MIDI
# protocol. If a device receives this packet and supports the MIDI spec, it is
# required to reply with an Identity Reply packet containing its manufacturer
# ID, family, and model version.  Hex Stream: F0 7E 7F 06 01 F7
#
# F0 — Start of SysEx (SOX)
# 7E — Universal Non-Real-Time ID (universal utility packet, not vendor-locked)
# 7F — Device ID / Broadcast (targets all connected devices or is a wildcard)
# 06 — Sub-ID 1 (General Information Category)
# 01 — Sub-ID 2 (Identity Request Function Code)
# F7 — End of SysEx (EOX)#

0xF0 0x7E 0x7F 0x06 0x01 0xF7

# vim: sw=4 ts=4 wm=4 et ft=dosini
